<%- include('partials/header') %>
<article class="form-card">
  <h1><%= title %></h1>
  <p><strong>Draft:</strong> This notice requires legal and deployment review before publication.</p>
  <% if (page === 'privacy') { %>
    <h2>Operator and contact</h2>
    <p>Michael Dunga operates Wende Nyasaye on a swiftener.com subdomain. For privacy requests, contact <a href="mailto:michaeldunga1@gmail.com">michaeldunga1@gmail.com</a> or <a href="tel:+254717953381">+254 717 953 381</a>.</p>
    <h2>Information and use</h2>
    <p>Accounts contain an email address and password hash. Favorites, bookmarks, notes and tags are stored to provide your hymn features. Notes and tags are private to the account, but administrators and those with database access may have access. The session cookie maintains sign-in and form protection. The server and hosting infrastructure may process technical information such as IP addresses and request logs for operation and security.</p>
    <h2>Hosting and access</h2>
    <p>The planned host is Contabo, on a VPS in the European Union. Information may be processed outside Kenya. Administrators and hosting or infrastructure providers may process information as needed to operate the service. Links and browser sharing features may involve third-party services with their own policies.</p>
    <h2>Retention and your choices</h2>
    <p>Account information, favorites and bookmarks remain until removed; operational logs and backups may be retained separately. Regular users can delete their accounts and saved items from Profile, and administrators can delete regular accounts. Contact the operator to request access, correction or deletion, or to raise other privacy concerns. Backup and log retention periods must be confirmed before deployment.</p>
    <p>Favorites and hymn data may also be cached on your device for offline use. Signing out clears local favorites on that device; deleting an account elsewhere does not immediately clear another device's storage. Clear browser storage to remove cached data.</p>
    <p>Applicable Kenyan data protection law may give you additional rights and allow complaints to the Office of the Data Protection Commissioner. Requests and cross-border safeguards will be handled in accordance with applicable law.</p>
  <% } else if (page === 'terms') { %>
    <h2>Using the hymnal</h2>
    <p>Wende Nyasaye provides a hymn directory and personal saved items. Use it lawfully, protect your account credentials, and do not disrupt the service or access another person's account without permission.</p>
    <h2>Content and availability</h2>
    <p>Hymn information is entered by administrators and may contain errors. Lyrics, compositions and other third-party material remain subject to their applicable rights; no permission to reuse them is implied. Administrators should only add material they have permission to reproduce. The service may change or become unavailable. Nothing here excludes rights that cannot lawfully be excluded.</p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Contact Michael Dunga at <a href="mailto:michaeldunga1@gmail.com">michaeldunga1@gmail.com</a> or <a href="tel:+254717953381">+254 717 953 381</a> with questions or content concerns.</p>
  <% } else { %>
    <h2>Session cookie</h2>
    <p>Wende Nyasaye uses the <code>connect.sid</code> session cookie to maintain sign-in and protect forms. It is a session cookie; signing out ends the server session. Blocking cookies may prevent account features from working.</p>
    <h2>Offline storage</h2>
    <p>A service worker caches the hymn directory and offline application files. The browser's local storage can hold the last signed-in user's favorites on that device; signing out clears them on that device. Bookmarks and their notes are not available offline. Browser settings can clear cookies, local storage and cached site data; clearing them disables offline access until the app is visited online again.</p>
    <p>See the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> for contact and data details. Infrastructure or future features may introduce additional storage and require an updated notice.</p>
  <% } %>
</article>
<%- include('partials/footer') %>
